.TH fmt 1 (date) "GNU coreutils (unreleased)"
.SH NAME
fmt \- simple optimal text formatter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY fmt
.RI [\f[B]\-\f[] WIDTH ]
.RI [ OPTION \~.\|.\|.\&]
.RI [ FILE \~.\|.\|.\&]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" Add any additional description here
.PP
Reformat each paragraph in the FILE(s), writing to standard output.
The option \fB\-WIDTH\fR is an abbreviated form of \fB\-\-width\fR=\fI\,DIGITS\/\fR.
.PP
With no FILE, or when FILE is \-, read standard input.
.PP
Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#fmt\-c
\fB\-c, \-\-crown\-margin\fP
.UE
preserve indentation of first two lines
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#fmt\-p
\fB\-p, \-\-prefix=\,STRING\fP
.UE
reformat only lines beginning with STRING,
reattaching the prefix to reformatted lines
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#fmt\-s
\fB\-s, \-\-split\-only\fP
.UE
split long lines, but do not refill
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#fmt\-t
\fB\-t, \-\-tagged\-paragraph\fP
.UE
indentation of first line different from second
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#fmt\-u
\fB\-u, \-\-uniform\-spacing\fP
.UE
one space between words, two after sentences
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#fmt\-w
\fB\-w, \-\-width=\,WIDTH\fP
.UE
maximum line width (default of 75 columns)
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#fmt\-g
\fB\-g, \-\-goal=\,WIDTH\fP
.UE
goal width (default of 93% of width)
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/fmt#fmt\-\-help
\fB\-\-help\fP
.UE
display this help and exit
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/fmt#fmt\-\-version
\fB\-\-version\fP
.UE
output version information and exit
